Gundeck can again store presences in PostgreSQL: the presence store is
selectable via `gundeck.presenceStore` (`redis` (default) or `postgresql`)
or the `GUNDECK_PRESENCE_STORE` environment variable.  When PostgreSQL is
selected, configure `gundeck.config.postgresql` (plus `postgresqlPool`,
and optionally `secrets.pgPassword`) like brig's postgresql settings; the
`redis-ephemeral` release and its TLS certificates are then unnecessary.
